<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Kitts</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saint Christopher Island</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Kitts, formally Saint Christopher, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-warner">Thomas Warner</a> founded the first English colony in the Caribbean there in 1623, and the French settled in 1625; the two partitioned the island in 1627. It was the base for further English and French colonisation and passed wholly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1713.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-kitts.jpg" alt="Saint Kitts" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Burmesedays · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Kitts_and_Nevis_Regions_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
